Dual License for Software and Aggregate Scientific Assets (EPJC / SCOAP3 Compatible)
====================================================================================

This repository accompanies the manuscript:
  "Non-monotonic benefits of physical target centering in conditional models
   of pion momentum loss"
submitted to The European Physical Journal C (EPJC).

1. Software and Source Code — MIT License
   Applies to all Python modules, scripts, tests, and build utilities
   (`src/`, `scripts/`, `tests/`, `protocol/*.py`, `reproduce.py`,
   `verify_saved_diagnostics.py`, and presentation rendering scripts).

2. Aggregate Scientific Data, Tables, Figures, and Documentation — CC-BY-4.0
   Applies to all aggregate JSON/CSV summaries, saved bootstrap replicate
   arrays (`bootstrap_replicates.npz`), protocol/provenance JSON manifests,
   compiled PDFs, vector/raster figures, LaTeX manuscript text/tables, and
   Markdown documentation, matching the SCOAP3 Creative Commons Attribution 4.0
   International (`CC BY 4.0`) open-access license of Eur. Phys. J. C.

3. Third-Party Typesetting Macro Notice
   The bundled Springer SVJour3 document class and bibliography style files
   (`svjour3.cls`, `svepjc3.clo`, `svglov3.clo`, `spphys.bst`) under
   `manuscript/representation_v2/epjc_submission/` remain the property of
   Springer Nature / LaTeX Project under their standard journal author-template
   distribution terms and are included solely for standalone LaTeX compilation.

